# Docker-first implementation (all plans)

All new coding and plan implementation for Bio-NAS must be designed to run **inside the Docker container** (`docker/Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yml`), not as host-only workflows.

## Do this

- Prefer extending `scripts/docker_entrypoint.py`, `docker/requirements.txt`, compose env/volumes, and scripts the container already invokes.
- Add Python deps to `docker/requirements.txt` (and ensure `Dockerfile` `COPY`s new scripts) instead of assuming host `pip install`.
- When a plan adds executable work, include Docker run/repro steps (`docker compose up --build` or equivalent) and expected outputs on the mounted volume (e.g. `./data/tcga` → `/data/tcga`).
- Point newcomers at [`docker/README.md`](../../docker/README.md) for the current compose contract.

## Do not do this

```text
# ❌ BAD — host-only path with no container story
python scripts/my_new_etl.py   # documented only for local venv

# ✅ GOOD — same script, wired for the container
# - add/invoke from scripts/docker_entrypoint.py (or compose command)
# - pin deps in docker/requirements.txt
# - document: docker compose up --build  → outputs on host mount
```

## Exceptions (document as out-of-container)

Only when impossible in-container (interactive DUA/browser account setup, ethics approvals, controlled-access downloads requiring human credentials). Mark those steps explicitly **outside Docker** in the plan/inventory; keep open/reproducible pieces in Compose.

